# Mobile App Shell — Student UI Design Contract

The student-facing UI is a **native mobile app shell rendered in a web page**, installable as a **PWA**. It is NOT a responsive website. Every component must look and behave like a native mobile app.

## Layout rules

- **Target viewport**: 360px wide. Max container width: `max-w-[420px]`.
- **Desktop behaviour**: centered phone-frame column on a dark/blurred background. No sidebars, no multi-column, no wider breakpoints.
- **Full-height screens**: `min-h-[100dvh]` using dynamic viewport height. Content scrolls within the frame.
- **Safe areas**: respect `env(safe-area-inset-*)` for notch/punch-hole devices.

## Navigation patterns (mobile-native, not web)

- **Top app bar**: 56px height, title + optional right-side action icons. No hamburger menus.
- **Bottom tab bar**: 64px height, fixed to bottom. Primary sections (Library / Progress / Profile). Active tab uses filled icon + label.
- **Screen transitions**: horizontal slide for forward/back navigation. Fade for tab switches.
- **No browser-style navigation**. No breadcrumbs, no top nav links. Back arrow in the app bar or swipe-back gesture.

## Interaction patterns

- **Tap targets**: minimum 44×44px for all interactive elements. Prefer 48×48px.
- **Cards**: rounded corners (12–16px), subtle shadows, used for list items and content blocks.
- **Bottom sheets**: for secondary actions, filters, details. Snappable to half/full height. Drag handle at top.
- **Full-screen modals**: for focused flows (onboarding steps, quiz review, settings). Slide up from bottom.
- **No web-style dialogs**, dropdowns, or hover tooltips. Use sheets, action menus, and inline expansion.
- **Pull-to-refresh**: for catalog and progress screens.

## Touch & gesture behaviour

```css
/* Apply to the app shell root */
-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
touch-action: manipulation;    /* disable double-tap zoom */
overscroll-behavior: none;     /* prevent browser pull-to-refresh bounce;
                                  pull-to-refresh on catalog/progress screens
                                  is a CUSTOM JS implementation (touch events),
                                  not the native browser gesture */
user-select: none;             /* on interactive elements, not text content */
-webkit-user-select: none;
```

## Typography & spacing

- System font stack: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif`.
- Base font size: 16px (prevents iOS zoom on input focus).
- Spacing: 8px grid (8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48).
- Line height: 1.4–1.5 for body, 1.2 for headings.

## PWA requirements

- `public/manifest.json` with `"display": "standalone"`, `"orientation": "portrait"`.
- `<meta name="theme-color">` matching the app bar background.
- `<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">`.
- `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">`.
- App icons (192×192, 512×512) and splash screens.

## What NOT to do

- ❌ No `@media (min-width: 768px)` or wider breakpoints for layout changes.
- ❌ No sidebars, multi-column grids, or wide desktop layouts.
- ❌ No hover-only interactions (hover states are fine as enhancement, never as the only way).
- ❌ No browser-style `<select>` or `<dialog>`. Use custom mobile pickers and sheets.
- ❌ No horizontal scroll containers wider than 420px.
- ❌ No tiny (< 44px) tap targets.

